+# Reviewed list of scanner suppressions and scanner-config files. One file, one place a reviewer reads. Format: path:rule:value:reason
+#   value = count@sha256: the number of markers of that rule in that file, then the sha256 of the sorted marker line texts (a widened or
+#   replaced marker changes the hash; the same text moved to another line does not). For scanner-config-file it is the sha256 of the file's bytes.
+#   A marker or config file that is not listed here, or whose count or hash differs, fails tools/scan_repo.py (the `check` job).
+#   Write this file with `python tools/scan_repo.py --print-list > new.txt`, never by hand, then read every line that changed.
+# BASELINE (main 2742c1b, 2026-11-09): the baseline lines were taken mechanically from the files as they were; they were NOT reviewed one
+#   by one (each marker keeps its own inline reason in the code). The baseline stays "review pass planned". Lines added or changed after it
+#   (marked "PR91" in the reason) were read by a reviewer in their PR. Every line added or changed later must be reviewed in its PR.
+#   `--print-list` gives a new line the placeholder reason "NEW, needs a reviewed reason"; the scan REFUSES it (and any reason shorter than 15
+#   characters) until a reviewer writes a real one.
+# Real enforcement of who may edit this file needs CODEOWNERS plus a ruleset: .github/CODEOWNERS names the reviewers, the ruleset that makes
+#   the review mandatory is an owner-only GitHub setting and is NOT done here. Until then this list is a review aid, not a lock.
